From 394dffef017b26ccb76f4b3353eedc9a7cbbf182 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 18:11:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 03/22] drm/gma500: load the SGX545 firmware from debugfs

On Cedarview, add dri/N/sgx/load. Writing to it fetches sgx545_ukernel.fw,
places its buffers in the SGX address space with the DDK heap layout, maps them
write-combined through a private page directory (the one the EDM will use) and
builds them for that layout. The buffers and the layout can be read back from
dri/N/sgx to check them against the reference loader. Nothing touches the SGX
registers yet, and nothing happens at probe.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
